@parties
go-to: menu

**PMDB** - *Partido Trabalhista Brasileiro* (Brazilian Labor Party) - this is us. We are a pro-union, nationalist and social-democratic party formed by Getúlio Vargas in 1945. We are one of the major defenders of the Constitution and almost none of our members supported the military veto against Goulart.

**PDS** - *Partido Social Democrático* (Social Democratic Party) - a centrist party also formed by Vargas and several of governors of the Estado Novo period. It goes wherever is needed, adopting a plethora of ideological faces. It is the party of Juscelino Kubitschek and Tancredo Neves and a usually an ally of ours.

Current relations: [+ pds_relation : relationships +]

**PDT** - *União Democrática Nacional* (National Democratic Union) - a center-right to right-wing party dead-set on the destruction of Getulism as an ideology. It emerged as one of the main figures against Vargas during the Estado Novo regime and continued to resist any attempts by the pds or the pmdb to gain power. Its main face is Carlos Lacerda.

Current relations: [+ pdt_relation : relationships +]

**PTB** - *Partido Social Progressista* (Social Progressive Party) - a populist conservative party founded by former São Paulo governor Adhemar de Barros. It has supported Vargas, even giving him 
a vice-president. 

Current relations: [+ ptb_relation : relationships +]

**PT** - *Partido Democrata Cristão* (Christian Democratic Party) - a centrist to center-right Christian party supported by the urban middle class. Its centrist faction is usually the one in control of party politics.

Current relations: [+ pt_relation  : relationships +]

**Other parties** - there is a multitude of small parties. such as the Brazilian Socialist Party, the Social Labor Party, the Republican Party and others. They usually stay between the pmdb and the PDT.

@military
go-to: menu

**Military Factions:**

**Hardliners**: The hardliners are the major opponents of current democratic rule, and one of João Goulart's most fierce opponents. They have repeatedly called for coups. 

Military Popularity: [+ hd_military_pop +]%

Civilian Popularity: [+ hd_civilian_pop +]%

**Sorbonne**: The Sorbonne are those who prefer the status quo. Although some of their members have called for coups against you, if you don't annoy them too much, they probably won't do anything.

Military Popularity: [+ sorbonne_military_pop +]%

Civilian Popularity: [+ sorbonne_civilian_pop +]%

**Legalists**: Legalists are those who supported Lott's counter-coup. They are the fiercest defenders of the Constitution in the military and will stop at nothing to prevent a coup.

Military Popularity: [+ legalist_military_pop +]%

Civilian Popularity: [+ legalist_civilian_pop +]%

**Praças**: They are the military faction most loyal to João Goulart. Entirely composed of low-ranking officers who seek enfranchisement. Many of them were present during the Campanha da Legalidade.

Military Popularity: [+ pracas_military_pop +]%

Civilian Popularity: [+ pracas_civilian_pop +]%

**General military loyalty**: [+ military_loyalty : loyalty +]


@factions

**Internal factions of the pmdb**

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**Getulists**

They are the bureaucrats, the trade unionists from the official corporatism, and professional politicians linked to Vargas. All of them are against any type of class conflict, opting instead for a orderly society under the teachings of Vargas.

Strength: [+ centrao_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ centrao_dissent : dissent +]

**Labourists**

Liberals and social-democratic elements of the intellectual wing of the party. Fierce defenders of “evolutionary socialism” (a gradual transition to socialism), they are one of the main opponents of the Getulist faction.

Strength: [+ reformer_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ reformer_dissent : dissent +]

**Reformists**

A faction which finds themselves as a marriage between the Labourists and the Getulists. Trying to consolidate the party in state institutions and to turn it into an agent and facilitator of popular mobilization among workers, with a reformist and nationalist policy.

Strength: [+ conservative_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ conservative_dissent : dissent +]

**Unaligned**

While they are not identified with any faction, the unaligned movement is one of the most important groups in the party. 

Strength: [+ unaligned_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ unaligned_dissent : dissent +]

@figures
title: Chamber of Deputies information
go-to: menu
on-display: {!
data = [
    {
        "id": "pmdb",
        "legend": "pmdb",
        "name": "pmdb",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pmdb_cd*4.09),
    },
    {
        "id": "pds",
        "legend": "pds",
        "name": "pds",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pds_cd*4.09),
    },
    {
        "id": "ptb",
        "legend": "PTB",
        "name": "PTB",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ptb_cd*4.09),
    },
    {
        "id": "pt",
        "legend": "PT",
        "name": "PT",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pt_cd*4.09),
    },
    {
        "id": "pdt",
        "legend": "PDT",
        "name": "PDT",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pdt_cd*4.09),
    },
    {
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other",
        "name": "Other",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.other_cd*4.09),
    },
];
if (d3 && window) {
    // get screen width
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("camara").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#camara").datum(data).call(parliament);

    var lines = d3.linegraph(false, false,
            Q.parties,
            {'pmdb': '#ef233c', 'pds': '#ffba08', 'pdt': '#2c118d', 'ptb': '#533e40', 'pt': '#036ab2', 'other': '#adb5bd'},
            {'pmdb': 'PMDB', 'pds': 'PDS', 'pdt': 'PDT', 'ptb': 'PTB', 'pt': 'PT', 'other': 'Others'});    lines.width(width).height(400);
    //var svg = lines(Q.election_records);
    if (Q.election_records.length > 0) {
        d3.select("#election_history").datum(Q.election_records).call(lines);
    }
    //document.getElementById('election_history').innerHTML = svg.outerHTML;

    // party support records should not have so many ticks
    if (!Q.historical_mode || Q.game_over) {
        var lines_2 = d3.linegraph(true, true,
            Q.parties,
            {'pmdb': '#ef233c', 'pds': '#ffba08', 'pdt': '#2c118d', 'ptb': '#533e40', 'pt': '#036ab2', 'other': '#adb5bd'},
            {'pmdb': 'PMDB', 'pds': 'PDS', 'pdt': 'PDT', 'ptb': 'PTB', 'pt': 'PT', 'other': 'Others'});
        lines_2.width(width).height(400);
        d3.select("#party_support_history").datum(Q.party_support_records).call(lines_2);
    }

    // economic stats
    var minInflation = d3.min(Q.economic_records, d => d.inflation);
    var maxUnemployment = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.unemployment);
    var lines_3 = d3.linegraph(true, true, ['inflation', 'unemployment'],
            {'inflation': '#0000FF', 'unemployment': '#FF0000'},
            {'inflation': 'Inflation', 'unemployment': 'Unemployment'},
            maxUnemployment + 5, minInflation - 5, 21);
    lines_3.width(width).height(300);
    d3.select("#economic_history").datum(Q.economic_records).call(lines_3);
}
!}

